;; Package board is a TamaGo board for whim's monitor (vmm/, doc/GUEST.md):
;; the runtime hooks of GOOS=tamago (runtime/goos) answered as the C guest
;; answers its host -- by hypercalls through the doorbell -- or in the
;; guest where an exit would cost too much.
;;
;;	CPUInit        cpuinit (boot_ISA.s): the monitor's entry state taken
;;	               (guest/abi), SSE on (amd64) or FP and
;;	               SIMD (arm64), the first stack, the runtime's rt0
;;	Hwinit0        goos.Bloc, the heap's start, at RamStart past the image
;;	Hwinit1        goos.Exit and goos.Idle set
;;	Nanotime       the counter (TSC; CNTVCT_EL0), at the rate the monitor
;;	               said (amd64) or CNTFRQ_EL0 says (arm64), from the
;;	               host's wall clock at the entry (R11; X6): in the guest,
;;	               since the scheduler asks it often; TamaGo's runtime
;;	               takes it for the wall clock too
;;	Printk         a line buffered, then abi.Message to stderr: a call
;;	GetRandomData  abi.Random: a call
;;	InitRNG        nothing
;;	Exit           abi.Exit: a call, which never returns
;;	Idle           one vCPU: abi.CPUPark to near the deadline, then a spin
;;	               to it, there being no interrupt to wait for -- or, once
;;	               the program has named an event area (EventArea), until
;;	               an event; several: a spin, then abi.CPUPark
;;	RamStart, RamSize, RamStackOffset
;;	               the monitor's, in registers at the entry
;;	Task, Wake, ProcID
;;	               on several vCPUs (smp.go): abi.CPUStart, abi.CPUWake
;;	               and abi.CPUSelf
;;
;; No interrupts, no timer: the runtime schedules its goroutines
;; cooperatively on each vCPU, and a vCPU only stops in a hypercall.  An
;; exception goes through the monitor's IDT to whim_vectors, which reports
;; it by abi.Fault as the C guest's vectors do.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.box.board) (go/file "board.go" :doc "Package board is a TamaGo board for whim's monitor (vmm/, doc/GUEST.md):\nthe runtime hooks of GOOS=tamago (runtime/goos) answered as the C guest\nanswers its host -- by hypercalls through the doorbell -- or in the\nguest where an exit would cost too much.\n\n\tCPUInit        cpuinit (boot_ISA.s): the monitor's entry state taken\n\t               (guest/abi), SSE on (amd64) or FP and\n\t               SIMD (arm64), the first stack, the runtime's rt0\n\tHwinit0        goos.Bloc, the heap's start, at RamStart past the image\n\tHwinit1        goos.Exit and goos.Idle set\n\tNanotime       the counter (TSC; CNTVCT_EL0), at the rate the monitor\n\t               said (amd64) or CNTFRQ_EL0 says (arm64), from the\n\t               host's wall clock at the entry (R11; X6): in the guest,\n\t               since the scheduler asks it often; TamaGo's runtime\n\t               takes it for the wall clock too\n\tPrintk         a line buffered, then abi.Message to stderr: a call\n\tGetRandomData  abi.Random: a call\n\tInitRNG        nothing\n\tExit           abi.Exit: a call, which never returns\n\tIdle           one vCPU: abi.CPUPark to near the deadline, then a spin\n\t               to it, there being no interrupt to wait for -- or, once\n\t               the program has named an event area (EventArea), until\n\t               an event; several: a spin, then abi.CPUPark\n\tRamStart, RamSize, RamStackOffset\n\t               the monitor's, in registers at the entry\n\tTask, Wake, ProcID\n\t               on several vCPUs (smp.go): abi.CPUStart, abi.CPUWake\n\t               and abi.CPUSelf\n\nNo interrupts, no timer: the runtime schedules its goroutines\ncooperatively on each vCPU, and a vCPU only stops in a hypercall.  An\nexception goes through the monitor's IDT to whim_vectors, which reports\nit by abi.Fault as the C guest's vectors do.\n" :imports [


